      "body": "\n        <p>MCP4SH v1.1.11 is mostly about making the current ST Haptics baseline cleaner, calmer, and more reliable across titles.</p>\n        <p>The main practical difference is not a new headline effect. It is the way the existing effects now separate under load: suspension impact behaviour is less likely to become a constant bed, Brake Feel and ABS/Lock are clearer, and Engine &amp; Tyres has more readable articulation without changing the intended front/rear drivetrain balance.</p>\n        <p>This release also tightens the setup and release path: updated profile assets, initial layout preset groundwork, safer license input handling, unified TytoSensoryLabs local state storage, OneDrive Documents support, and the first public-facing TCR language.</p>\n        <p>In plain terms: this is intended to be a stronger, calmer baseline rather than a louder one.</p>\n      "
